.TH KAGI-CLUSTER-HOST 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-cluster-host \- run or administer a distributed Kagi node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kagi-cluster-host
.RB [ \-c " " \fIFILE\fR ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a Kagi node or performs an administrative operation using its node YAML.
The node owns its local data directories and participates in Raft for
authoritative metadata.
The normal runtime requires at least six configured hosts with at least six
disks per host.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Read node configuration from
.IR FILE .
The default is
.IR /etc/kagi/node.yaml .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the command list, or use
.I command
.B \-\-help
for command-specific arguments.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the node API, metadata service, configured listeners, and background
controllers for health, repair, maintenance, and snapshots.
.TP
.B status
Print the local node and cluster summary as JSON.
.TP
.B audit
Validate the configured security policy and print its effective configuration
as JSON without starting the daemon.
.TP
.BI "put " "KEY FILE"
Store the bytes in
.I FILE
as a new version of
.IR KEY .
.TP
.BI "get " "KEY OUTPUT"
Retrieve the current object and write its bytes to
.IR OUTPUT .
.TP
.BI "locate " KEY
Print the current fragment placement for an object.
.TP
.BI "repair " KEY
Repair missing or damaged fragments using the object's protection policy.
.TP
.BI "scrub " KEY
Verify fragment checksums and readability.
.TP
.BI "clear-health " RESOURCE
Clear the resource's flap and quarantine state after confirming that it is
safe to return to service.
.TP
.BI "generate-pq-identity \-\-public " PUBLIC " \-\-secret " SECRET
Write an ML-DSA-87 identity pair.
This command can run before node YAML exists.
Keep the private key restricted to the node operator and service.
.TP
.BI "web-user-add " USER " \-\-password-file " FILE
Create or update a local console account.
Use
.BI \-\-role " viewer"
(the default) or
.BR "\-\-role admin" .
The password is read from a file to keep it out of command arguments.
.TP
.BI "membership add node " ID " \-\-endpoint " URL
Add a voting node on the current Raft leader.
Optional flags are
.BI \-\-site " SITE" ,
.BI \-\-rack " RACK" ,
and
.BR "\-\-pq-public-key FILE" .
.TP
.BI "membership remove " "node|rack|site ID"
Remove the named voter or all voters with the named rack or site label.
Run this on the current Raft leader.
Batched rack and site additions use the membership REST endpoint.
.SH OPERATIONS
Kagi records authoritative metadata changes through Raft.
The runtime supports replication and Reed-Solomon, LRC, product-matrix MSR,
and CLAY erasure coding.
CLAY is the default erasure family.
Supported builds can use optional accelerators for the data transforms.
.PP
The REST service handles operations beyond the local CLI, including volume
management, snapshot operations, and capacity changes.
When
.B web_console.enabled
is set, the operations console is available under
.BR /ui .
Protect the browser login and session traffic with TLS.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-config (1),
.BR kagi-host (1),
.BR kagi-install (1),
.BR kagi-volume-nbd (1)
